        "uuid": "00076109_945bdc41",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/ApplicationSelfCertifiedNetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 152,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-17T06:31:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this not a little bit bizarre in terms of builder usage ? Normally a builder has public setters and lets you build an object tailored to your needs.\n\nHere, the way you create an instance of ApplicationSelfCertifiedNetworkCapabilities is to call the factory method, which makes sense, but somehow there is still this Builder with a public constructor, a public getter, a public build() method, and that\u0027s it.\n\nIf the builder is not used by the caller to build the object, then it\u0027s only as useful as what it contains, and in this case the only thing it contains is a long.\n\nI think you\u0027d be better served by just removing the Builder class, move parseXml to the parent class, and have the long a local in parseXml, to be |\u003d with every call to parseDeclarationTag (which could just return the value).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 152,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 152,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "51c19b8ec839592907cb4c3c01bfc5bc36c0164c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
